From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:48:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: v4l2-ctrls: give the AVS sequence control a valid
 default

validate_avs_sequence() refuses a zero horizontal_size or vertical_size,
but the default value of V4L2_CID_STATELESS_AVS_SEQUENCE left both at
zero. A driver's current value was therefore invalid until userspace set
one, and VIDIOC_TRY_EXT_CTRLS on the current values failed with -EINVAL
(v4l2-compliance: "try_ext_ctrls returned an error (22)").

Default to QCIF, as the AVS2 sequence control does.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ctrls-core.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ctrls-core.c b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ctrls-core.c
index 9837ee1b1520..5cb2e3217e43 100644
--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ctrls-core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ctrls-core.c
@@ -219,8 +219,10 @@ static void std_init_compound(const struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl, u32 idx,
 	case V4L2_CTRL_TYPE_AVS_SEQUENCE:
 		p_avs_sequence = p;
 
-		/* 8-bit 4:2:0 progressive JiZhun profile */
+		/* 8-bit 4:2:0 progressive JiZhun profile, QCIF */
 		p_avs_sequence->profile_id = V4L2_AVS_PROFILE_JIZHUN;
+		p_avs_sequence->horizontal_size = 176;
+		p_avs_sequence->vertical_size = 144;
 		p_avs_sequence->chroma_format = 1;
 		p_avs_sequence->sample_precision = 1;
 		p_avs_sequence->flags =
